Why 

Since you're a DevOps Engineer and already work with Docker, Kubernetes, Jenkins, AWS, and CI/CD, you should learn Helm from the perspective of building, packaging, deploying, and maintaining production Kubernetes applications.



Helm Learning Roadmap (Beginner → Expert)


Phase 1: Understand Why Helm Exists

Without Helm:

	kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
	kubectl apply -f service.yaml
	kubectl apply -f ingress.yaml
	kubectl apply -f configmap.yaml
	kubectl apply -f secret.yaml

	Imagine 50 YAML files.

Helm solves this by packaging Kubernetes manifests.

Think:

	APT  -> Linux packages
	NPM  -> Node packages
	PIP  -> Python packages
	Helm -> Kubernetes packages



Phase 2: Install Helm

	helm version 

	Add repository

		helm repo add bitnami https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami

		helm repo list 

		helm repo update # updates the current repos data 

	# search the charts display the details of chart 

	helm search repo nginx




Phase 3: First Helm Deployment

	Install nginx

		helm install my-nginx bitnami/nginx

	Check it 

		helm list

	check all in default namespace 

		kubectl get all

	Uninstall above charts 

		helm uninstall my-nginx




Phase 4: Helm Architecture

	Helm
	│
	├── Chart
	├── Release
	├── Repository
	└── Values


	Chart:

		Package of Kubernetes manifests.

		Example:

			nginx-chart/


	Release:

		Installed chart.

		Example:

			helm install my-nginx nginx-chart

			release name: 
				my-nginx

	Repository:

		Chart storage.

		Example:

			Bitnami
			ArtifactHub
			Internal Repo

	Values:

		Configuration file.

		Example:

			replicaCount: 3
			image:
			  tag: latest


Phase 5: Create Your First Chart

	helm create myapp


	Generated structure:

		myapp
		│
		├── Chart.yaml
		├── values.yaml
		├── charts/
		├── templates/
		└── templates/tests/


Phase 6: Important Files

	Chart.yaml

		Metadata

		apiVersion: v2
		name: myapp
		version: 1.0.0



	values.yaml

		User configuration

			replicaCount: 2

			image:
			  repository: nginx
			  tag: latest


	templates/

		Contains manifests

			deployment.yaml
			service.yaml
			ingress.yaml

Phase 7: Helm Template Syntax

	Variable

		{{ .Values.replicaCount }}

		Example

			replicas: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}

	values.yaml

		replicaCount: 5

		Output

			replicas: 5


Phase 8: Deploy Custom Chart

	Render templates

		helm template myapp .


	Install

		helm install myapp .

	Upgrade

		helm upgrade myapp .

	Delete

		helm uninstall myapp


Phase 9: Values Override

	Default

		replicaCount: 1


	Override

		helm install myapp . --set replicaCount=5

	or 

		helm install myapp . -f prod-values.yaml


Phase 10: Environment-Based Deployments

	Development

		helm install myapp . -f values-dev.yaml

	Production

		helm install myapp . -f values-prod.yaml

	Structure

		values-dev.yaml
		values-qa.yaml
		values-stage.yaml
		values-prod.yaml

Phase 11: Helm Upgrade

	Upgrade image

		helm upgrade myapp . --set image.tag=v2


	History

		helm history myapp


Phase 12: Rollback

	View revisions

		helm history myapp


	Rollback

		helm rollback myapp 1

	Very important interview topic.


Phase 13: Helm Hooks

	Run jobs before deployment.

	Example:

		annotations:
		  "helm.sh/hook": pre-install


	Hooks:

		pre-install
		post-install

		pre-upgrade
		post-upgrade

		pre-delete
		post-delete

		Used for:

			DB migrations
			Backup jobs
			Health checks



Phase 14: ConfigMaps


	values.yaml

		env:
		  APP_MODE: production

	configmap.yaml

		data:
		  APP_MODE: {{ .Values.env.APP_MODE }}


Phase 15: Secrets

	values.yaml

		secret:
		  password: mypass

	secret.yaml

		data:
		  password: {{ .Values.secret.password | b64enc }}



Phase 16: Conditional Deployments

	Deploy ingress only if enabled.

	values.yaml

		ingress:
		  enabled: true

	Template

		{{ if .Values.ingress.enabled }}
		...
		{{ end }}



Phase 17: Loops

	values.yaml

	ports:
	  - 80
	  - 443

	Template

		{{ range .Values.ports }}
		- containerPort: {{ . }}
		{{ end }}

Phase 18: Helpers

	templates/_helpers.tpl

		{{ define "app.name" }}
		myapp
		{{ end }}

	Use

		{{ include "app.name" . }}


Phase 19: Dependencies

	Install Redis with app.

	Chart.yaml

	dependencies:
	  - name: redis
	    version: 18.x.x
	    repository: https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami

	Download

		helm dependency update


Phase 20: Package Chart

	Package

		helm package .

	Output

		myapp-1.0.0.tgz


Phase 21: Linting

	Validate chart

		helm lint .

	Interview favorite command.



Phase 22: Dry Run


	helm install myapp . --dry-run

	Render only

		helm template .



Phase 23: Debugging


		helm install myapp . \
		--debug


	View values

		helm get values myapp

	View manifests

		helm get manifest myapp



Phase 24: Production Best Practices


	Use Separate Values


		values-dev.yaml
		values-qa.yaml
		values-stage.yaml
		values-prod.yaml
		Never Store Secrets

	Use:

		HashiCorp Vault
		Sealed Secrets
		External Secrets Operator
		CI/CD

	Jenkins Pipeline

		stage('Deploy') {
		    sh '''
		    helm upgrade --install myapp . \
		    -f values-prod.yaml
		    '''
		}




Phase 25: Expert Topics

	Learn these deeply:

		Helm Template Functions
		Sprig Functions
		Named Templates
		Subcharts
		Library Charts
		OCI Registries
		Chart Versioning
		Helm Hooks
		Helm Testing
		GitOps Integration